{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_011tCFUMgSedCNgmBDktoaY9","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Paper Framing — trace-verdict-study\n2\t\n3\t## Target Venue\n4\t- Primary: EMNLP 2026 Main (ARR submission)\n5\t- Fallback: EMNLP 2026 Findings\n6\t- Deadline: ARR May 25, 2026 (10 days from today)\n7\t\n8\t## Core Insight\n9\t\n10\tTrace SFT effectiveness depends critically on **trace granularity matching task output entropy**: verdict tasks (1-bit output) benefit from execution traces, but compact, decision-relevant abstractions (VOTA: 99.2%) dramatically outperform full traces (81.8%). The performance gradient no_trace (75.1%) < full_trace (81.8%) < VOTA (99.2%) shows that the \"right\" trace is not \"more trace\" — it's the minimal information sufficient to determine the verdict, providing higher information density per token. All conditions verified on v5 codebase with consistent eval pipeline.\n11\t\n12\t## Core Claims (≤3)\n13\t\n14\t1. **VOTA dramatically improves verdict prediction**: Verdict-Optimized Trace Abstraction provides +24.0pp accuracy improvement over no-trace baseline (99.2% vs 75.1%) for test outcome prediction, 95% CI [+21.9, +26.8] excluding zero. Plan_001 confirms this is genuine behavioral understanding, not trivial actual/expected string comparison (vota_no_ae: 99.4%).\n15\t\n16\t2. **Trace compression significantly improves verdict accuracy over full traces**: Full execution traces achieve 81.8% (+6.6pp, CI [+4.4, +9.0]), but VOTA achieves 99.2% (+24.0pp) — a +17.4pp advantage. Plan_002 (label-only loss) 量化因果分解：gradient dilution 贡献 ~26% of gap (4.5pp, 修复后 full_trace 86.2%), information overload 贡献 ~74% (13.0pp, 只有 trace compression 能解决)。\"Even with oracle loss masking that eliminates gradient dilution, full traces still underperform VOTA by 13pp, confirming that information density — not training signal distribution — is the primary bottleneck.\" 所有条件基于 v5 代码版本公平对比。\n17\t\n18\t3. **Information granularity, not information presence, determines trace SFT value**: Through systematic ablation — removing assertion-point information from VOTA (plan_001 减法) and isolating exception/loop components individually — we establish a **component importance hierarchy** for verdict-optimized trace design, providing empirical design principles at the compression-component level. [注：ae_only 88% fallback 污染，不支撑 element-level 归因。ae_only 结果移至 Appendix 附 caveat；主线证据为 plan_001 减法 + exception_only + loop_only 三角验证。]\n19\t\n20\t## Story Spine\n21\t\n22\t- **Problem**: Existing trace SFT studies (DCSH, TracePile) evaluate only generative tasks and find limited benefit. No prior work has tested trace SFT on code behavior verdict tasks (binary pass/fail), nor designed trace representations specifically for classification.\n23\t\n24\t- **Existing approaches & gaps**: DCSH (EMNLP Findings 2025) tested 5 trace formats on generation tasks, finding limited benefit. TracePile (NeurIPS 2025) scaled to 2.6M samples but only evaluated generation. TRACED (ICSE 2024) showed traces help encoder-based classification, but nobody has tested decoder SFT. All existing trace formats are designed for full execution simulation, not classification.\n25\t\n26\t- **Our framing**: We ask \"does trace granularity need to match task complexity?\" and demonstrate that verdict tasks — with O(1) output entropy — benefit from a fundamentally different trace design principle than generation tasks. VOTA captures only decision-relevant execution states (assertion snapshots, exception summaries) rather than full simulation.\n27\t\n28\t- **Headline result template**: \"On test verdict prediction, VOTA-SFT achieves 99.2% (+24.0pp over baseline), outperforming both no-trace (75.1%) and full-trace SFT (81.8%) — a clear performance gradient demonstrating that decision-relevant trace compression, not more trace information, maximizes SFT effectiveness for classification.\"\n29\t\n30\t## Venue Fit Risks\n31\t\n32\t- EMNLP主会 vs SE: 论文核心贡献是对 trace SFT 的 task-dependent 效果的系统性实证发现 + 新 trace representation，属于 NLP for code 方向。投 EMNLP Code track 合适。\n33\t- 单任务风险: 目前只在 test verdict prediction 一个任务上验证。需要至少加一个 verdict task（patch correctness 或 bug detection）才够 EMNLP Main。Findings 可能只需当前结果 + ablation。\n34\t- Leakage concern: 如果 ablation 证明 VOTA 效果主要来自 actual==expected 字符串比对，claim 需要调整为 \"verdict tasks 需要的不是 trace reasoning 而是 decision-relevant data points\"——仍然 publishable 但 framing 不同。\n35\t\n36\t## Contingency Framing\n37\t\n38\t### Claim 1 contingency — RESOLVED (D008)\n39\t\n40\t**实际结果**: vota_no_ae accuracy 99.41% vs VOTA 完整版 99.16%（差异 3 样本/1190，不显著）。去除 actual/expected 后准确率不降反微升。\n41\t\n42\t**生效 framing**: \"genuine behavioral understanding\" — VOTA 的效果来自 exception + loop + assertion 结构性信息，不依赖 actual/expected 字符串比对。VOTA teaches execution-grounded verdict reasoning。\n43\t\n44\t**残余问题**: trace 结构性信号（[No trace available]→fail, [ERROR]→fail, [ASSERT]+[LOOP]→pass）可能构成 trivial pattern。此问题对所有 VOTA 变体等同存在。plan_003 exception_only ablation 将量化 [ERROR] 信号贡献。需在论文 Discussion 中诚实讨论。\n45\t\n46\t### Claim 2 contingency — RESOLVED (D006 + D009)\n47\t\n48\t**实际结果**: v5 full_trace 81.8%（collapse 为 bug, D006）。plan_002 label-only loss 86.2%，量化 gradient dilution 为 minor factor：4.5pp/17.4pp = 26% (D009)。\n49\t\n50\t**生效 framing**: \"Both trace types help verdict tasks, but VOTA's advantage is primarily information quality (74% of gap), not training signal distribution (26%). Even with oracle loss masking that eliminates gradient dilution, full traces still underperform VOTA by 13pp — trace compression is not just cost-saving but accuracy-improving through higher information density per token.\"\n51\t\n52\t## Key Open Questions (Post-MVP)\n53\t\n54\t1. ~~actual/expected ablation~~ (已解决: D008, genuine behavioral understanding 路径确认)\n55\t2. ~~full_trace collapse~~ (已解决: chat template bug, D006) → plan_002 改为 ablation: label-only loss 能否进一步提升 full_trace 81.8%?\n56\t3. 能否在第二个 verdict task 上复现？→ 决定 generalization claim\n57\t4. 需要多模型验证吗？→ 时间允许就加 DeepSeek-Coder\n58\t\n59\t## Anticipated Reviewer Concerns\n60\t\n61\t| Concern | Planned Response |\n62\t|---------|-----------------|\n63\t| \"VOTA 99.2% 可能是 trivial actual==expected 比对\" | plan_001 已否定：去 ae 后 99.41%，不降反升。VOTA 效果来自 exception/loop/assertion 结构 |\n64\t| \"VOTA 高 accuracy 可能来自 trace 结构性信号（error 有无、trace 有无）而非深层理解\" | plan_003 exception_only 将量化 [ERROR] 信号贡献；Discussion 中诚实讨论结构性信号角色；full_trace 也有这些信号但仅 81.8%，说明结构性信号不是全部 |\n65\t| \"只在一个任务/数据集上测试\" | 加 patch correctness task 或 CRUXEval verdict variant |\n66\t| \"只用一个模型\" | 加 DeepSeek-Coder-6.7B 复现（DCSH 同模型） |\n67\t| \"full_trace collapse 可能是实现 bug\" | 诚实披露：v2 collapse 确为 chat template bug；v5 修复后 full_trace 81.8%，三条件层次清晰。论文报告 v5 结果，Appendix 记录 bug 发现过程作为方法论透明性 |\n68\t| \"VOTA 只是 feature engineering 不是方法创新\" | 定位为 empirical contribution: 系统性发现 + design principles + task-spectrum analysis |\n69\t| \"与 DCSH 的关系不清\" | 明确：我们 complement DCSH（他们做 generation，我们做 classification） |\n70\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"612a8978-6776-487f-b7a9-cd63d9b39a17","uuid":"411c3385-8e11-420a-a091-5522c0668362","timestamp":"2026-05-15T09:17:07.133Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0509_4/projects/trace-verdict-study/artifacts/dream_reports/dream_20260515T084908/worst/paper_framing.md","content":"# Paper Framing — trace-verdict-study\n\n## Target Venue\n- Primary: EMNLP 2026 Main (ARR submission)\n- Fallback: EMNLP 2026 Findings\n- Deadline: ARR May 25, 2026 (10 days from today)\n\n## Core Insight\n\nTrace SFT effectiveness depends critically on **trace granularity matching task output entropy**: verdict tasks (1-bit output) benefit from execution traces, but compact, decision-relevant abstractions (VOTA: 99.2%) dramatically outperform full traces (81.8%). The performance gradient no_trace (75.1%) < full_trace (81.8%) < VOTA (99.2%) shows that the \"right\" trace is not \"more trace\" — it's the minimal information sufficient to determine the verdict, providing higher information density per token. All conditions verified on v5 codebase with consistent eval pipeline.\n\n## Core Claims (≤3)\n\n1. **VOTA dramatically improves verdict prediction**: Verdict-Optimized Trace Abstraction provides +24.0pp accuracy improvement over no-trace baseline (99.2% vs 75.1%) for test outcome prediction, 95% CI [+21.9, +26.8] excluding zero. Plan_001 confirms this is genuine behavioral understanding, not trivial actual/expected string comparison (vota_no_ae: 99.4%).\n\n2. **Trace compression significantly improves verdict accuracy over full traces**: Full execution traces achieve 81.8% (+6.6pp, CI [+4.4, +9.0]), but VOTA achieves 99.2% (+24.0pp) — a +17.4pp advantage. Plan_002 (label-only loss) 量化因果分解：gradient dilution 贡献 ~26% of gap (4.5pp, 修复后 full_trace 86.2%), information overload 贡献 ~74% (13.0pp, 只有 trace compression 能解决)。\"Even with oracle loss masking that eliminates gradient dilution, full traces still underperform VOTA by 13pp, confirming that information density — not training signal distribution — is the primary bottleneck.\" 所有条件基于 v5 代码版本公平对比。\n\n3. **Information granularity, not information presence, determines trace SFT value**: Through systematic ablation — removing assertion-point information from VOTA (plan_001 减法) and isolating exception/loop components individually — we establish a **component importance hierarchy** for verdict-optimized trace design, providing empirical design principles at the compression-component level. [注：ae_only 88% fallback 污染，不支撑 element-level 归因。ae_only 结果移至 Appendix 附 caveat；主线证据为 plan_001 减法 + exception_only + loop_only 三角验证。]\n\n## Story Spine\n\n- **Problem**: Existing trace SFT studies (DCSH, TracePile) evaluate only generative tasks and find limited benefit. No prior work has tested trace SFT on code behavior verdict tasks (binary pass/fail), nor designed trace representations specifically for classification.\n\n- **Existing approaches & gaps**: DCSH (EMNLP Findings 2025) tested 5 trace formats on generation tasks, finding limited benefit. TracePile (NeurIPS 2025) scaled to 2.6M samples but only evaluated generation. TRACED (ICSE 2024) showed traces help encoder-based classification, but nobody has tested decoder SFT. All existing trace formats are designed for full execution simulation, not classification.\n\n- **Our framing**: We ask \"does trace granularity need to match task complexity?\" and demonstrate that verdict tasks — with O(1) output entropy — benefit from a fundamentally different trace design principle than generation tasks. VOTA captures only decision-relevant execution states (assertion snapshots, exception summaries) rather than full simulation.\n\n- **Headline result template**: \"On test verdict prediction, VOTA-SFT achieves 99.2% (+24.0pp over baseline), outperforming both no-trace (75.1%) and full-trace SFT (81.8%) — a clear performance gradient demonstrating that decision-relevant trace compression, not more trace information, maximizes SFT effectiveness for classification.\"\n\n## Venue Fit Risks\n\n- EMNLP主会 vs SE: 论文核心贡献是对 trace SFT 的 task-dependent 效果的系统性实证发现 + 新 trace representation，属于 NLP for code 方向。投 EMNLP Code track 合适。\n- 单任务风险: 目前只在 test verdict prediction 一个任务上验证。需要至少加一个 verdict task（patch correctness 或 bug detection）才够 EMNLP Main。Findings 可能只需当前结果 + ablation。\n- Leakage concern: 如果 ablation 证明 VOTA 效果主要来自 actual==expected 字符串比对，claim 需要调整为 \"verdict tasks 需要的不是 trace reasoning 而是 decision-relevant data points\"——仍然 publishable 但 framing 不同。\n\n## Contingency Framing\n\n### Claim 1 contingency — RESOLVED (D008)\n\n**实际结果**: vota_no_ae accuracy 99.41% vs VOTA 完整版 99.16%（差异 3 样本/1190，不显著）。去除 actual/expected 后准确率不降反微升。\n\n**生效 framing**: \"genuine behavioral understanding\" — VOTA 的效果来自 exception + loop + assertion 结构性信息，不依赖 actual/expected 字符串比对。VOTA teaches execution-grounded verdict reasoning。\n\n**残余问题**: trace 结构性信号（[No trace available]→fail, [ERROR]→fail, [ASSERT]+[LOOP]→pass）可能构成 trivial pattern。此问题对所有 VOTA 变体等同存在。plan_003 exception_only ablation 将量化 [ERROR] 信号贡献。需在论文 Discussion 中诚实讨论。\n\n### Claim 2 contingency — RESOLVED (D006 + D009)\n\n**实际结果**: v5 full_trace 81.8%（collapse 为 bug, D006）。plan_002 label-only loss 86.2%，量化 gradient dilution 为 minor factor：4.5pp/17.4pp = 26% (D009)。\n\n**生效 framing**: \"Both trace types help verdict tasks, but VOTA's advantage is primarily information quality (74% of gap), not training signal distribution (26%). Even with oracle loss masking that eliminates gradient dilution, full traces still underperform VOTA by 13pp — trace compression is not just cost-saving but accuracy-improving through higher information density per token.\"\n\n## Key Open Questions (Post-MVP)\n\n1. ~~actual/expected ablation~~ (已解决: D008, genuine behavioral understanding 路径确认)\n2. ~~full_trace collapse~~ (已解决: chat template bug, D006) → plan_002 改为 ablation: label-only loss 能否进一步提升 full_trace 81.8%?\n3. 能否在第二个 verdict task 上复现？→ 决定 generalization claim\n4. 需要多模型验证吗？→ 时间允许就加 DeepSeek-Coder\n\n## Anticipated Reviewer Concerns\n\n| Concern | Planned Response |\n|---------|-----------------|\n| \"VOTA 99.2% 可能是 trivial actual==expected 比对\" | plan_001 已否定：去 ae 后 99.41%，不降反升。VOTA 效果来自 exception/loop/assertion 结构 |\n| \"VOTA 高 accuracy 可能来自 trace 结构性信号（error 有无、trace 有无）而非深层理解\" | plan_003 exception_only 将量化 [ERROR] 信号贡献；Discussion 中诚实讨论结构性信号角色；full_trace 也有这些信号但仅 81.8%，说明结构性信号不是全部 |\n| \"只在一个任务/数据集上测试\" | 加 patch correctness task 或 CRUXEval verdict variant |\n| \"只用一个模型\" | 加 DeepSeek-Coder-6.7B 复现（DCSH 同模型） |\n| \"full_trace collapse 可能是实现 bug\" | 诚实披露：v2 collapse 确为 chat template bug；v5 修复后 full_trace 81.8%，三条件层次清晰。论文报告 v5 结果，Appendix 记录 bug 发现过程作为方法论透明性 |\n| \"VOTA 只是 feature engineering 不是方法创新\" | 定位为 empirical contribution: 系统性发现 + design principles + task-spectrum analysis |\n| \"与 DCSH 的关系不清\" | 明确：我们 complement DCSH（他们做 generation，我们做 classification） |\n","numLines":70,"startLine":1,"totalLines":70}}}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01FEDwikeVxoMwsUxHqiMcfP","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Now I have a clear picture of both the experiment data and the paper framing. Let me also check if the output directory exists.\n\nThe narrative guidance for \"worst\" tier is clear:\n- exception_only ≈ VOTA (no statistical significance), proving VOTA's 99.2% is essentially error flag extraction, not execution-grounded reasoning\n- loop compression has no contribution (≈ no_trace)\n- ae signal is moderate but has fallback contamination\n- trivial rule (has_ERROR→fail) reaches 93%, close to exception_only\n- Must reframe from \"behavioral understanding\" to \"What Makes Traces Work for Verdict Tasks? An Empirical Decomposition\"\n\n\n- Claim 3 completely fails, Claim 1 significantly weakened, Claim 2 unaffected\n- The key insight is that full_trace also leverages the ERROR signal but only reaches 81.8%, revealing information overload is the real problem — yet the solution isn't intelligent compression but simply isolating that error flag\n\nNow I'm writing the LaTeX paper, covering all the ablations from the experiments: exception_only as the core finding showing equivalence to VOTA, loop_only demonstrating no value, ae_only showing moderate but contaminated gains, the trivial rule baseline hitting 93% without any training, plus the cross-model replication and no-trace variants.\n\nI need to map out the full experimental suite: cross-model baselines with DeepSeek Coder across different trace configurations, the DebugBench transfer results, trace length ablations at various cutoffs, calibration metrics, and seed robustness checks. The paper structure will flow from main results through component ablations, then cross-model validation, generalization to DebugBench, and finally the analysis sections on trace length and calibration.\n\nThe framing is shifting toward an honest empirical story—VOTA's effectiveness comes from extracting error signals rather than deep behavioral reasoning, which I'll present as the core finding in the title and throughout the discussion.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":12854,"cache_read_input_tokens":23173,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":12854},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"612a8978-6776-487f-b7a9-cd63d9b39a17","uuid":"6ec128f8-38e7-4bf1-8e67-773907736591"}
